 Radiological Sciences (J.E.S., D.S.C., P.D.C.)."}, {"affiliation": "Center for Artificial Intelligence in Diagnostic Medicine (D.S.C., R.S.T., P.D.C.), University of California, Irvine, Orange, California."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7385-8532"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0001-7645-7865"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-0460-7884"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-2359-7394"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-4565-2614"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-0817-8770"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-1664-3580"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics", "supporting_data"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "1", "volume": "42", "journalIssueId": 3090099, "dateOfPublication": "2021 Jan", "monthOfPublication": 1, "yearOfPublication": 2021, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "AJNR Am J Neuroradiol", "title": "AJNR. American journal of neuroradiology", "essn": "1936-959X", "issn": "0195-6108", "isoabbreviation": "AJNR Am J Neuroradiol", "nlmid": "8003708"}, "printPublicationDate": "2021-01-01"}, "pubYear": "2021", "pageInfo": "2-11", "abstractText": "Artificial intelligence technology is a rapidly expanding field with many applications in acute stroke imaging, including ischemic and hemorrhage subtypes. Early identification of acute stroke is critical for initiating prompt intervention to reduce morbidity and mortality. Artificial intelligence can help with various aspects of the stroke treatment paradigm, including infarct or hemorrhage detection, segmentation, classification, large vessel occlusion detection, Alberta Stroke Program Early CT Score grading, and prognostication. In particular, emerging artificial intelligence techniques such as convolutional neural networks show promise in performing these imaging-based tasks efficiently and accurately. The purpose of this review is twofold: first, to describe AI methods and available public and commercial platforms in stroke imaging, and second, to summarize the literature of current artificial intelligence-driven applications for acute stroke triage, surveillance, and prediction.", "affiliation": "From the Departments of Radiological Sciences (J.E.S., D.S.C., P.D.C.).", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["review-article", "Review", "Journal Article"]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Artificial Intelligence"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Triage", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Stroke", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "DG", "qualifierName": "diagnostic imaging"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Neuroimaging", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.3174/ajnr.A6883"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC7814792"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC7814792?pdf=render"}, {"availability": "Free", "availabilityCode": "F", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.3174/ajnr.a6883"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "N", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 151, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": 